# Canonical site URL — used for metadata, sitemap.xml and robots.txt.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://harinexglobal.com

# --- Contact form delivery --------------------------------------------
# The /api/inquiry route validates every submission and delivers it as soon
# as one provider below is set. With neither set it returns delivered:false
# and the UI shows the visitor a mailto fallback, so nothing is ever
# silently dropped. SMTP wins if both are present.

# GMAIL (works today, no domain needed)
# Requires 2-Step Verification on the account, then an App Password from
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords — a normal Gmail password will
# NOT work. Strip the spaces Google shows in the 16-character password, and
# URL-encode the @ in the address as %40:
# SMTP_URL=smtps://harinexglobal%40gmail.com:abcdefghijklmnop@smtp.gmail.com:465

# RESEND (needs a verified sending domain — use once the domain is live)
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Where inquiries land. Defaults to CONTACT.email in lib/content.ts.
# Change this one line to move from Gmail to company mail later.
# INQUIRY_TO=hello@harinexglobal.com

# From address. Leave unset with Gmail SMTP: Gmail rewrites the sender to
# the authenticated mailbox anyway, so the default matches what arrives.
# INQUIRY_FROM=HariNex Global Website <hello@harinexglobal.com>

# --- Analytics --------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Web Analytics is already live. Its token is checked into
# components/site/analytics.tsx rather than set here, because it is public
# by design — it ships in the HTML of every page and names the site, not a
# visitor. Nothing to configure.
#
# Set this only to point a staging build at a different property. Note that
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined at BUILD time, so it takes a rebuild.
# The beacon never renders outside production builds either way.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef

# --- Hari AI fallback (optional) --------------------------------------
# The chat assistant answers from its built-in knowledge base for free and
# needs neither of these. When nothing matches a question it says so and
# offers the contact form.
#
# Set BOTH to enable the AI fallback, which answers off-topic questions
# from the site's own content instead. It is only invoked when the
# knowledge base misses, so most conversations still cost nothing — but
# messages that do reach it are billed per token.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAT_AI=true
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- Social publishing (optional) --------------------------------------
# Only scripts/publish-social.mjs reads these, and only to send posts that
# a person has already marked "approved" in social/queue.json. Without them
# the publisher names each unconfigured platform and skips it.
#
# In production these live in GitHub repository secrets, not in a file:
# Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions. The scheduled workflow at
# .github/workflows/social-publish.yml maps them in at run time.
#
# Set them here only to test a live post from your own machine.

# LinkedIn — company page posting. Needs a LinkedIn app with the
# Community Management API, and the ORG_URN of the company page
# (urn:li:organization:143089961 for HariNex Global).
# LINKEDIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# LINKEDIN_ORG_URN=urn:li:organization:143089961

# Facebook Page — a long-lived Page access token, not a user token.
# FACEBOOK_PAGE_ID=
# FACEBOOK_PAGE_TOKEN=

# Instagram — the Business account id linked to that Facebook Page.
# Uses FACEBOOK_PAGE_TOKEN above; a personal IG account cannot post via API.
# INSTAGRAM_BUSINESS_ID=

# X — write access is a paid tier. Leave unset to keep X manual; the
# publisher will skip it and say so rather than failing the run.
# X_BEARER_TOKEN=
